# Build-time configuration for the deployed tc.41chan.net bundle.
#
# RECOVERED FROM VESPER 2026-08-15, where Technetium was developed and where
# this file already existed -- untracked, so a rebuild anywhere else silently
# fell back to the in-repo DEVWEB defaults and broke login with "redirect_uri is
# not allowed for this client". Tracked now so the build config travels with the
# code instead of living on one machine.
#
# No secrets here: a public OAuth client id and two URLs, all readable in any
# built bundle.

VITE_MAS_CLIENT_ID=000000000000000000000TCWEB
VITE_HOMESERVER=https://41chan.net

# Native Simplified Sliding Sync (MSC4186). Explicit here so the prod build does
# not depend on the machine-local .env.local. Flip to 0 + redeploy to revert.
VITE_SLIDING_SYNC=1

# VITE_MEDIA_BASE is deliberately absent. It pointed the client at the
# fourier-auth gateway for media; media now goes to the homeserver's own
# authenticated-media endpoint, the same URL Element uses, so the variable has
# no reader left. Left documented rather than silently dropped, because seeing
# it on vesper and not here should not read as an oversight.

# End-to-end encryption for DIRECT MESSAGES is ON in every build, and there
# is no flag for it here any more (operator, 2026-10-05: "E2EE is defaulted to
# ON and the passphrase box in settings allows it to be turned OFF"). The one
# off switch is per browser, under Manage session, behind the passphrase
# (src/client/e2eeOptIn.ts). One tab per device is enforced
# (src/client/deviceLock.ts), which is what made default-on safe.

# Domain mode is OFF for this build. Launch is imminent and it is not ready
# (operator, 2026-09-21); it stays in the tree and is simply not offered,
# because a feature nobody can reach ships better than one ripped out in a
# hurry. A dev server has it without setting anything; on the deployed site the
# per-browser toggle in Settings turns it on for one browser
# (src/client/domainMode.ts). Flip this to 1 when it is ready for everyone.
#
# Only the exact string "1" counts. 0, false and empty are all off, on purpose:
# a truthiness test here would put an unfinished feature in front of everybody.
VITE_DOMAIN=0
